      influences: 'Hegelian and idealist philosophy, the Bible, and a long exposure to Indian religious thought during his years as a judge in the Punjab.',
      influenced: 'Ernest Holmes, who called him a decisive influence on Science of Mind; Genevieve Behrend, who studied with him directly and popularised his ideas; and, at one remove, most of the subsequent movement.',
