      influences: 'The Hermetic and Rosicrucian streams of Central European occultism; elemental theory inherited from Renaissance magic; his own naturopathic practice, which shows in the attention to the body.',
      influenced: 'A dispersed body of serious practitioners, and later Hermetic teachers who take his graded structure as a model. He has never been fashionable, which he would probably have counted as a good sign.',
