      imageVsRecord: 'He is often read as a mystic. He insisted on describing himself as an empiricist working from clinical observation, though his later writing on alchemy and synchronicity is unmistakably speculative. His conduct during the 1930s, including his role in a German-dominated psychotherapy body and some statements of the period, remains a subject of serious criticism.',
