      'Michael Singer was a doctoral student in economics in Florida when a spontaneous experience of inner silence in 1971 redirected his life. He took up yoga and meditation, founded the Temple of the Universe, and — improbably — also built a large medical software company, which is the subject of his second book. He writes without lineage claims or Sanskrit, in the plainest available English.',
