      'His subject is the arithmetic of ordinary days. He argued that outcomes are not produced by dramatic decisions but by small actions repeated — and, crucially, that the same arithmetic applies to neglect. The missed walk, the unread page, the postponed conversation compound exactly as the disciplines do, and neither shows a result for a long time, which is why both are so easy to sustain.',
