    example: {
      title: 'Applied to loneliness that will not resolve',
      scenario: 'Someone has done the reasonable things — friendships, work, therapy — and still carries an ache that nothing quite meets. Most advice treats this as a problem of insufficient connection. Rumi treats it as information. The reed cries because it was cut from the reed bed; the longing is not evidence that something is wrong with the life but that the self is oriented towards something it has not found in it. His counsel would not be to accept the loneliness passively or to spiritualise it into contentment. It would be to stop running from the ache, let it be a form of prayer, and see what it is actually pointing at. This will suit some people profoundly and will strike others as evasion, and both responses are worth taking seriously.',
    },
